  "worked_solution": "From part 3, we have the function $p(x)=-6{x}^{2}+360x.$\n\nWe substitute $x=24$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(24) & =-6(24)^{2}+360(24) \\\\  & =-3\\,456+8\\,640 \\\\  & =5\\,184\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the company will earn $$5\\,184.$",
